"""Immutable acceptance contract for the sustained travel vertical slice."""
CONTRACT = '''Build Aster Journeys, a real local DEMONSTRATION travel product. No live bookings, payments or external network. Python stdlib + SQLite backend, vanilla HTML/CSS/JS frontend. All persistence is server SQLite at db_path. Each handle(request,db_path) runs in a fresh networkless process. Close connections and COMMIT writes. Native dict response {status:int,body:dict}; request={method,path,body,headers}. Never JSON encode body. Browser calls await window.furyApi(method,path,body={}) -> {status,body}; no fetch/libraries. The trusted bridge stores returned login/register body.token and sends request.headers.authorization='Bearer '+token; frontend need not store tokens. All user/private and admin authorization MUST be enforced by backend, never trust user_id/role in body. Use salted hashlib.pbkdf2_hmac passwords, secrets.token_urlsafe sessions persisted in SQLite with expiry. Seed demo administrator admin@example.test / DemoAdmin2028! (label public demo credentials); registration ALWAYS creates ordinary user. Invalid input400, unauthenticated401, forbidden403, missing404, conflict409, created201, successful GET/update/delete200. Nonempty body.error on errors. No raw tracebacks, password hashes or session tokens in lists.
Architecture uses these flat files: db.py exports connect(db_path) initializing schema and deterministic inventory, auth.py exports user(conn,request) -> dict or None and routes(conn,request) -> response or None, catalog.py/private.py/reservations.py each routes(conn,request) -> response or None. backend.py handle opens with contextlib.closing(db.connect(db_path)) as conn, conn: dispatches auth,catalog,private,reservations; returns404 if no route. modules import db/auth as needed. Every row factory is sqlite3.Row. Every routes(conn,request) MUST first check its owned path and method and return None for unrelated requests BEFORE authentication. In particular private.routes must not intercept /quote or unknown routes with401. All schema in db.py: users(id,email UNIQUE,password,salt,role), sessions(token PRIMARY KEY,user_id,expires), listings(id,name,city,country,description,price INTEGER EUR/night,capacity INTEGER,active INTEGER), favorites(user_id,listing_id,UNIQUE(user_id,listing_id)), itineraries(id,user_id,title,notes), reservations(id,user_id,listing_id,check_in,check_out,party,total INTEGER,request_key,UNIQUE(user_id,request_key)). Use parameterized SQL. No Python global persistence. Backend handles invalid JSON types safely.
API contract:
GET /health -> {ok:true,demo:true}.
POST /register {email,password} -> {token,user:{id,email,role}}; password min10 max128, normalized email max160 valid; duplicate409.
POST /login same response, invalid credentials401. POST /logout deletes bearer session ->200. Logout is idempotent: repeating logout with an already revoked bearer may return200 or401. Verify actual revocation with GET /me and protected GET /favorites returning401 for the revoked token, not by prescribing a repeated-logout status. GET /me -> {user} or401.
GET /listings accepts a native dict body EVEN THOUGH its method is GET; POST /listings is not a supported route and returns404. Example handle request: {"method":"GET","path":"/listings","body":{"sort":"price_desc"},"headers":{}}. GET /listings body filters {q,city,sort:'price_asc'|'price_desc',page:1,page_size:6,max_price,party} -> {listings:[...],total,page,page_size}; server filter case-insensitive name/city/country q, city exact, max_price finite positive, party integer1..8, page_size1..12. Defaults page1/page_size6. GET /listings/{id} -> {listing}. Seed >=18 rich fictional properties across Lisbon, Kyoto, Copenhagen, Edinburgh, Porto, Ljubljana, with varying numeric EUR prices and capacities. All labelled demo. No fake ratings/availability.
GET /favorites -> {favorites:[listing records]} authenticated. POST /favorites {listing_id} ->201 (idempotent200 allowed). DELETE /favorites/{listing_id} ->200. Only own records.
GET /itineraries -> {itineraries:[{id,title,notes}]}. POST /itineraries {title,notes} ->201 {itinerary}. PUT /itineraries/{id} {title,notes} ->200 {itinerary}. DELETE same ->200. Authenticate; cross-user IDs404. Trim title1..100 notes<=4000.
POST /quote is PUBLIC: never require a session or bearer token. Anonymous requests must reach validation and return200 for valid input,400 for invalid input. POST /quote {listing_id,check_in,check_out,party} -> {quote:{listing_id,check_in,check_out,party,nights,nightly,total,currency:'EUR'}}. Real YYYY-MM-DD dates, check_in >= today, checkout>checkin, nights<=30, party integer1..capacity. Numeric finite fields; reject bool. Price comes ONLY from DB, total=nightly*nights (no invented fees). Unknown/inactive listing404.
POST /reservations same fields plus request_key string8..100 ->201 {reservation:{id,listing_id,check_in,check_out,party,total}}; authenticated; recompute quote server-side ignore supplied total. Duplicate request_key per user409. GET /reservations -> {reservations:[own records]}. GET /reservations/{id} ->{reservation}, own only otherwise404. Demo inventory permits concurrent illustrative reservations; do not imply live availability.
GET /admin/reservations -> {reservations:[sanitized records with user_id]}; GET /admin/listings -> {listings:[including inactive]}; PUT /admin/listings/{id} {price,active} ->{listing}. Admin only403 for ordinary users,401 anonymous. Price integer1..10000, active integer0/1. No arbitrary SQL/routes/files.
Frontend stable acceptance hooks: header span#user-display for signed-in email; #auth-buttons containing button#auth-nav.nav-link[data-view=auth] for Sign in; all navigation buttons use .nav-link and data-view=listings|favorites|itineraries|reservations|admin. Bind EVERY data-view control, including Back buttons. Delegated click handlers must select ALL supported action attributes in closest(), not only [data-view]; test each attribute separately before routing. Dataset IDs are strings: convert to integer API fields. Detail responses unwrap body.listing; rendering a detail must not recursively fetch or navigate to itself. #auth-section contains registration/login and is hidden for signed-in users. Do not show any technical request-key input; keys are automatic.  form#register-form fields name=email,password; form#login-form same; buttons#logout; input#search, select#city, select#sort, input#max-price, button#search-button; div#listing-list with article[data-listing-id] and buttons[data-detail], buttons[data-favorite]; button#next-page; section#listing-detail; form#quote-form fields name=listing_id,check_in,check_out,party; button#quote-button type=submit; #quote-result; button#reserve-button; #reservations; #favorites; form#itinerary-form fields name=title,notes; #itineraries with buttons[data-edit-itinerary] and [data-delete-itinerary]; section#admin contains #admin-reservations and form#inventory-form fields name=listing_id,price,active; #status role=status. Use readable errors in #status and disable pending actions. Show login user and hide admin for ordinary users, while backend enforces permissions. Reload retrieves persistent lists. Every section/navigation works. Provide working edit flow with same itinerary form. Quotes reset when inputs change; generate the unique request_key automatically and retain it for retries of the same submission. Never ask the user to invent an idempotency key. Reserve requires a current quote; double click guarded, duplicate conflicts visible. Detail populates quote listing ID. Search/filter/sort/pagination call backend. Responsive cards, deliberate loading/empty/error/success states, coherent premium travel visual design, locally authored SVG destination imagery (label illustrative). No placeholders/dead buttons or fake counts. Render numeric prices. No inline scripts/styles; index.html references styles.css/app.js. Use textContent or escape untrusted HTML.
'''
CRITERIA = [
 ('catalog','Server search, filters, sorting, details and bounded pagination'),
 ('auth','Registration, login, logout and persistent secure sessions'),
 ('private','Favorites, itinerary CRUD and two-user ownership'),
 ('reservation','Validated server quotes, persistent demo reservations, duplicate protection'),
 ('admin','Admin inventory editing and reservation visibility with backend permissions'),
 ('browser','Desktop/mobile real browser workflows, console and network checks'),
 ('restart','Database survives generated application restart'),
]
TASKS = [
 ('Travel architecture', 'architecture.md', 'Write a concise architecture, acceptance checklist and next actions. Follow the immutable schema/API exactly. No implementation claims.'),
 ('Travel database','db.py','Implement connect(db_path) only, exact immutable schema, repeatable CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS and deterministic INSERT OR IGNORE seeding >=18 varied rich listings. Seed each listing with an explicit stable integer primary ID; repeated connect() MUST NOT grow inventory or restore edited price/active values. Initialize the demo administrator with PBKDF2 password, salt. connect returns sqlite3.Connection row_factory=Row; commit initialization. No deleting existing records.'),
 ('Travel authentication','auth.py','Implement user(conn,request) and routes(conn,request) for register/login/logout/me. Exact contract/schema. PBKDF2 SHA256 100000 iterations, hex password/salt, constant-time compare, random session tokens and expiry timestamp. Must match db.py seeded admin password. user returns dict with id,email,role only. Only recognized auth routes return responses; others None. Catch duplicate email409. Never trust client role.'),
 ('Travel catalog','catalog.py','Implement routes(conn,request) for health, listing search/detail and admin listings/update. Use auth.user for admin authorization. Server SQL filters/order/pagination; exact contract. Validate types/ranges. Only recognized routes return responses else None.'),
 ('Travel private records','private.py','Implement routes(conn,request) for favorites and itinerary CRUD. Exact schema/contract. Ownership and validation on every operation. auth.user(conn,request). Return None outside owned routes.'),
 ('Travel reservations','reservations.py','Implement routes(conn,request) for quote/reservations/admin reservations. Exact schema/contract. Quote helper is PUBLIC with no authentication and performs all validation and calculates server price. Enforce bearer authentication/ownership for reservations and admin role for admin routes ONLY. Duplicate request_key409. Return None outside owned routes.'),
 ('Travel API integration','backend.py','Implement handle(request,db_path) with exact dispatcher contract. Import db,auth,catalog,private,reservations. Open/close SQLite safely, commit transaction before closing; errors400 for malformed values, no swallowed defects. Dispatch all modules returning first non-None, unknown404. No extra routes.'),
 ('Travel interface','index.html','Implement complete accessible semantic HTML for ALL stable hooks in immutable contract. Polished coherent premium travel workspace named Aster Journeys. Include demo notice, public demo admin credentials, navigation, login/register forms, search filters, card list, details/quote/reservations/favorites/itinerary CRUD/admin inventory form. Every control has accessible labels. No placeholder sections. app.js wires later. index.html only.'),
 ('Travel visual design','styles.css','Implement polished responsive light travel design: warm ivory, ink typography, teal actions, generous whitespace, premium cards with local SVG artwork from JS, sidebar/header, clear forms and states, mobile stacking at375px, no horizontal overflow. Read actual HTML. styles.css only.'),
 ('Travel browser behavior','app.js','Implement ALL frontend behavior and stable hooks in immutable contract using window.furyApi only. Read exact existing HTML and backend contract. Keep under22000 chars. No stub handlers. Render every required data-* hook, convert dataset IDs to numbers for JSON bodies, load actual private records on each navigation, and bind forms before awaiting session startup. Page boots listing discovery and GET /me; reload private state if authenticated. Login/register success bridge auto stores token; use returned user to reload private lists. Implement server filtering, pagination, detail, quote, reserve, favorites, itinerary create/edit/delete, logout, admin records and inventory update. Inline generated SVG destination scenes on cards, labelled illustrations. Handle errors visibly. FormData and explicit numeric conversions. No external network/dependencies. Use no browser storage for business data.'),
 ('Travel independent QA','test_backend.py','Implement unittest tests using backend.handle and tempfile DBs only. Cover exact auth, filtering, validation, two-user ownership, itineraries, quote arithmetic, persistence, duplicate request_key and admin enforcement. Use LOGIN for the seeded administrator, never re-register it. Success fixtures require request_key strings of8..100 characters. Test only the documented method/path contract. Itinerary retrieval is GET /itineraries (owned list), not GET /itineraries/{id}. Verify list isolation and cross-user PUT/DELETE404 without modifying the owner record. Derive listing prices and city counts from actual API records; exact per-city counts are not fixed. Keep tests concise; preserve meaningful assertions. Do not weaken requirements. Tests are supplemental to immutable acceptance.'),
]
